================================================================================
Community: full-height layout, clear erases preview, detect spinner & styling
================================================================================

Context:
The Community page content did not stretch to the bottom of the viewport
(violating the desktop bottom-alignment geometry in .cursor/11). The layout is
now structured with a direct-child .content-section, a left rail for Algorithm
and Materialized partition, and a full-height preview pane on the right that
aligns with the sidebar bottom. Clear graph now erases the preview. A spinner
is shown during detection. Button styles updated: Detect is primary blue,
Materialize is secondary grey.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/simulation/_sim_communities.html
   Direct-child .content-section; .comm-layout with .comm-rail and .comm-main;
   .comm-preview-loading spinner overlay; Detect changed to btn-primary (blue)
   and Materialize to btn-secondary (grey).
2. src/front/static/simulation/css/simulation.css
   Full-height flex layout (.comm-layout, .comm-rail, .comm-main,
   .comm-preview-card, .comm-preview-canvas, .comm-preview-loading) adhering
   to desktop bottom alignment; mobile media query resets.
3. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-communities.js
   _erasePreview() on clear graph; _showPreviewLoading() during detection;
   window resize listener for preview graph resizing.
4. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py
   Contract assertions for full-height structure, button classes, and loading
   overlay.

