================================================================================
Studio: highlight group neighborhood on collapsed group click
================================================================================

Context:
Clicking an entity in Studio dims the map and highlights incident
relationships and heritage edges. Clicking a collapsed group circle only
opened the member pane and skipped that highlight. Group click now reuses
the same neighborhood treatment for remapped edges on the super-node.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js
   highlightNeighborhood matches link endpoints by node id or name (group
   id !== name); group click opens the member pane, highlights by d.id, and
   marks the group node selected without entering mapSelectedEntityNames.
2. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-map.css
   Selected and dimmed styles for .map-group-circle.
3. tests/units/front/test_studio_views_groups_contract.py
   Contracts for group highlight call, id/name matching, and selected CSS.

